// t-contains-10: a union holding the very cell it is asked to contain binds
// that cell to a sibling member.
//
// `(Self::Set(s), t)` (graphix-types/src/typ/contains.rs:906) has no identity
// pre-pass, unlike the Set ⊇ Set arms (own-cell check 843-852, identity
// pre-pass 889-900), and set_commit (1124-1127) tries structural members
// before free ones. The TVar arms are skipped because 'y occurs in the set,
// so `[i64, 'y] ⊇ 'y` commits through `i64 ⊇ 'y` and binds 'y := i64.
// GRAPHIX_DBG_BIND=1 prints `SET-T [i64, '_N] >= '_N` then
// `BIND rhs '_N(..) := Primitive(.. I64)`.
// An identical structural member loses the same way:
// `[{v: i64}, {v: 'y}] ⊇ {v: 'y}` binds 'y := i64.
//
// command: graphix --check design/review-2026-10-05/repro/t-contains-10.gx
//
// expected: accepted. `[y, 1]` is Array<[i64, 'y]> and pushing y into it
//   needs nothing of 'y; `let f = |y| [y, 1]; f("s")` is accepted.
// observed (HEAD c722befe, debug build): refused at the call, far from the
//   cause:
//   in: "s"
//   type mismatch '_N: i64 does not contain string
//
// Other shapes, same bind (all refused, all accepted without the write):
//   let f = |y| array::concat([y, 1], [y]); f("s")
//   let f = |y, c: bool| { let x = select c { true => y, false => null };
//     x <- y; x }; f(1, true)         -- 'y := null
//   let f = |y, c: bool| { let x = select c { true => {v: y}, false => {v: 1} };
//     x <- {v: y}; x }; f("s", true)  -- the struct member case
// Declaring the parameter `|y: 'a|` (a rigid cell) is accepted.
//
// The bind can also make the checker ACCEPT a program it must refuse:
//   let c = 0;
//   let y = str::parse("42")$;
//   let x = select c { 0 => y, _ => null };
//   x <- y;
//   x
// `x <- y` binds parse's target to null, the sibling member, so the program
// runs and parse yields null (graphix-fuzz check: AGREE). Without `x <- y`
// it is refused: "the type 'b must be fully known here, a type-directed
// operation reads it: annotate it".
let f = |y| array::push([y, 1], y);
f("s")
